lowing effects of \"The Dragon that Devours the Dogma\" once per turn. If this card is Special Summoned: You can shuffle up to 2 cards from any GY(s) and/or banishment into the Deck. During the End Phase, if this card is in the GY because it was sent there this turn: You can add 1 \"Dogmatika\" or \"Tri-Brigade\" card from your Deck to your hand."},"78114463":{"role":"Sky Striker","quick":"Can be activated the turn it was Set by revealing another Set Trap; choose the LP mode deliberately."},"78199891":{"role":"Trap","quick":"While you control a Mikanko, target a face-up monster and equip an Equip Spell from Deck that can legally equip to it.","caution":"You need a Mikanko already on field. Rondo can equip to an opponent’s monster and immediately take it."},"79912449":{"role":"Spell","quick":"Equip an opposing monster, then control it while you control a Mikanko. It remains equipped under your control.","caution":"Both players are prevented from activating that monster’s effects while you control it. Losing Rondo sends the equipped monster to GY."},"80044027":{"role":"Equip Spell","quick":"Summons a Mikanko from hand or GY and equips it. Can optionally put a negated monster from their GY back on their field as a damage target.","caution":"Only one activation per turn. The optional opposing revival requires a legal GY target. Equipping it through Ohime is not the same as activating its summon effect."},"80843006":{"role":"Extra Deck tool","quick":"1 Spellcaster monster + 1 non-Spellcaster monster\r\nYou can target 1 face-up monster on the field and declare 1 Attribute; it becomes that Attribute. During your opponent's Main Phase (Quick Effect): You can Fusion Summon 1 Fusion Monster from your Extra Deck, by banishing this card you control and monsters from your field or GY as material. If this card is in your GY: You can declare 1 Attribute; this card in the GY becomes that Attribute until the end of this turn. You can only use each effect of \"Mixousia the Confounder\" once per turn."},"81196066":{"role":"2 Lunalights. If Fusion Summoned, searches Luna Light Perfume; can target another Lunalight card you control to return it to hand/Extra Deck, then optionally Special Summon a Lunalight from hand. Its GY banish reduces opposing ATK by original DEF.","quick":"21442"},"81260679":{"role":"LIGHT · Level 6 · ATK 0","quick":"Reveals herself to search a Mikanko card, then discards. Preparation finds her. Ceremony can bring her onto the field, where she can equip a suitable GY Equip Spell as a Quick Effect.","caution":"The discard happens during resolution, not as activation cost. She is Level 6, not a Rank 3 material. Ceremony does not properly Ritual Summon her."},"81439173":{"role":"GY access","quick":"Send one monster from Deck to GY. Limited to one."},"82344137":{"role":"Branded engine","quick":"You can reveal this card and 1 Spell/Trap in your hand; until the end of the next turn, neither player can activate cards or effects in response to the activation of cards, or effects of cards, with the revealed Spell/Trap's name. If this card is sent from the hand or field to the GY by a Spell/Trap effect: You can Special Summon this card. If this card is Special Summoned from the GY: You can take control of 1 monster your opponent controls with the highest ATK (your choice, if tied). You can only use each effect of \"Phara the Primordial Goddess\" once per turn."},"82489470":{"role":"Branded engine","quick":"When a monster declares an attack: You can Special Summon this card from your hand, and if you do, negate that attack, then, if you control a Fusion Monster that mentions \"Fallen of Albaz\" as material, you can destroy the monster that declared that attack. If a monster is banished face-up (except during the Damage Step): You can banish this card from your field or GY; Special Summon 1 LIGHT Spellcaster monster from your hand or GY whose ATK equals its own DEF. You can only use this effect of \"The Golden Swordsoul\" once per turn."},"83190280":{"role":"Pendulum revival","quick":"Pendulum effect revives a Lunalight from GY with its effects negated; it cannot attack and is destroyed during the End Phase."},"84550369":{"role":"Normal Spell","quick":"Sets up the GY and a Mikanko Spell/Trap. The doctrine’s first line sends Sanaki and sets Fire Dance.","caution":"Only one of its two effects can be used per turn. You cannot use the GY Ritual-summon effect later in the same turn as its normal effect. The normal effect restricts later Extra Deck summons."},"86066372":{"role":"Conditional · Link 4","quick":"Unicorn (3) + an extra Effect Monster (1) is legal when unlocked, and makes 5300 ATK through Unicorn. The previous list did not provide a reliable spare-body sequence for this ladder. Keep as an optional ladder payoff, never assume it is a routine finish.","caution":"At least two Effect Monsters totaling Link Rating 4. All generic routes require an unlocked turn."},"87209160":{"role":"GY access","quick":"Send itself from hand or field to GY to send a Level 3 or lower Beast, Beast-Warrior, or Winged Beast from Deck: Silver Hound is a key target."},"87746184":{"role":"Extra Deck tool","quick":"\"Fallen of Albaz\" + 1 LIGHT monster\r\nIf this card is Fusion Summoned: You can Fusion Summon 1 Level 8 or lower Fusion Monster from your Extra Deck, except \"Albion the Branded Dragon\", by banishing Fusion Materials mentioned on it from your hand, field, and/or GY. During the End Phase, if this card is in the GY because it was sent there this turn: You can add to your hand or Set 1 \"Branded\" Spell/Trap directly from your Deck. You can only use each effect of \"Albion the Branded Dragon\" once per turn."},"87931906":{"role":"Fusion","quick":"Fuse a Lunalight from hand/field. If your opponent controls a monster Special Summoned from the Extra Deck, you may also use one Lunalight from your Deck or Extra Deck."},"88753594":{"role":"3 Lunalights; once in GY, a later turn’s effect can boost a Fusion you control by 3000 ATK.","quick":"14185"},"90448279":{"role":"LIGHT · Rank 12 · ATK 3000","quick":"A field reset after an Xyz has battled. Overlay Downerd and retain its stacked materials.","caution":"Its effect sends your other cards too. You cannot use the ordinary Mikanko combo and simply add Zeus after battle under its Extra Deck restriction."},"90590303":{"role":"Rank 4 fallback. In Defense Position it changes face-up monsters to Defense and negates their activated effects when activated there, including yours.","quick":"13163"},"90673288":{"role":"Sky Striker","quick":"If Special Summoned that turn, searches in the End Phase for a Striker Spell whose name is absent from your GY. Resolve Multirole first when Setting Engage will free that name."},"93039339":{"role":"DARK · Rank 12 · ATK 2900","quick":"A one-body emergency Xyz when the opponent’s recent Extra Deck activity meets its condition.","caution":"The alternate summon ends your further Normal/Special Summons for the turn. Use your highest-ATK monster, not any arbitrarily chosen smaller monster."},"94145021":{"role":"Sky Striker","quick":"After a Deck-to-hand add, prevents further Deck-to-hand additions that turn."},"95515789":{"role":"Branded engine","quick":"If you control \"Fallen of Albaz\" or it is in your GY: You can Special Summon this card from your hand. During the Main Phase (Quick Effect): You can Fusion Summon 1 Level 8 or higher Fusion Monster from your Extra Deck, using monsters from your hand or field as material. During the End Phase, if a Fusion Monster(s) was sent to your GY this turn: You can add this card from the GY to your hand. You can only use each effect of \"Blazing Cartesia, the Virtuous\" once per turn."},"96381979":{"role":"Rank 4 that sets a Fire Formation from Deck; useful Tenki access after the Hound lock ends.","quick":"10407"},"96729612":{"role":"Spell","quick":"Finds Level 6 Ohime from Deck. The Ritual Spell recovery is optional and usually unused in this profile.","caution":"Preparation is not Pre-Preparation of Rites; they search differently."},"97165977":{"role":"Cat Dancer + a Lunalight; required name for Leo Dancer unless Chick supplies it.","quick":"12319"},"97268402":{"role":"Branded engine","quick":"During your opponent's Main Phase (Quick Effect): You can send this card from your hand to the GY, then target 1 Effect Monster your opponent controls; negate the effects of that face-up monster your opponent controls, until the end of this turn."},"98127546":{"role":"Conditional · Link 5","quick":"Example: your I:P (2) + Hu-Li (1) + Ha-Re (1) + an opposing Effect Monster (1). That is four actual bodies, totaling five. Three small Mikanko plus one ordinary opposing Effect Monster total only four, so are insufficient. Legal in special resource states, inefficient here.","caution":"At least four Effect Monsters totaling Link Rating 5; may use one opposing monster. All generic routes require an unlocked turn."},"98338152":{"role":"Sky Striker","quick":"Negates a face-up monster; at 3 Spells it can take control and occupy your Main Monster Zone."},"98462037":{"role":"Sky Striker","quick":"Needs two LIGHT and/or DARK monsters and converts material into targeted pressure."},"99550630":{"role":"Sky Striker","quick":"Destroys a face-up monster; at 3 Spells it may also destroy a Spell/Trap."}}}
